  "name": "Venomancer: Pendo's Charm and Acute Senses work natively (#1272, #1711)",
  "contract": "#1272, #1711: both are stock aura types. Acute Senses (300664 rank 1, 300665 rank 2) effects 0 and 2 are SPELL_AURA_MOD_TOTAL_STAT_PERCENTAGE on Intellect (misc 3) and Agility (misc 1) with bp 4/9 so 5/10 percent; its effect 1 is SPELL_EFFECT_DUMMY (3) carrying a Spirit misc value, so it applies no aura and Spirit must not move (the tooltip names only Intellect and Agility). Pendo's Charm (504400) is SPELL_AURA_MOD_RAGE_FROM_DAMAGE_DEALT (aura 213) of bp 14 so +15 percent, read in Unit::RewardRage. That function is reached only when HasActivePowerType(POWER_RAGE) holds; a Venomancer is a Mana class whose Rage pool exists in Beetle Form (Player::InitDataForForm sets POWER_RAGE for FORM_VENOMANCER_BEETLE), so the scenario asserts the aura amount and that melee in Beetle Form builds Rage. The exact 1.15 ratio has no deterministic metric (rage per hit follows the weapon damage roll), so it is asserted by amount, not by rate.",
